1.The Statement of Unaudited Consolidated Financial Results of Lloyds Metals and Energy Limited and its subsidiaries for the quarter ended 30 June 26 was approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on 10 August 26.2.The Consolidated Financial Results have been prepared in accordance with the recognition and measurement principles prescribed under Indian Accounting Standard 34 relating to Interim Financial Reporting under Section 133 of the Companies Act 13 read with the relevant rules and other generally accepted accounting principles in India.3.In accordance with Indian Accounting Standard 108 relating to Operating Segments the Group has four reportable operating segments namely Mining of Iron Ore Steel and related value added products MDO Operation and related services and Copper and related products. Segment information has been provided in accordance with Indian Accounting Standard 108.4.The Statutory Auditors have conducted a limited review of the financial results for the quarter ended 30 June 26 and have issued an unqualified report thereon.5.Under the Lloyds Metals and Energy Limited Employee Stock Option Plan 17 and Employee Stock Option Plan 24 the number of options exercisable at the beginning of the period on 1 April 26 was 184264. During the period 1220038 options were granted 415279 options vested 85013 options lapsed and 32245 options were exercised. The number of options outstanding at the end of the period on 30 June 26 was 6766112 and the number of options exercisable was 273323.6.Through warrant conversions during December 25 to March 26 the Company allotted 33695000 fully paid Equity Shares of face value  1 each to Promoters and Non Promoters. The allotments comprised 15268950 shares on 31 December 25 805500 shares on 3 February 26 and 17620550 shares on 13 March 26. The Company received  16207295000 as balance exercise price at  481 per Equity Share.7.On 30 January 26 the Company issued 60000 senior secured listed rated redeemable non convertible debentures through private placement. Each debenture had a face value of  1Lac aggregating to  600 Cr. The issue comprised a base issue of  300 Cr and a green shoe option of  300 Cr which was fully subscribed.8.During financial year 24 to 25 the Company issued 175Lacs Equity Shares of face value  1 each at  696 per Equity Share through Qualified Institutional Placement and raised  1218 Cr. Of this amount  916.13 Cr was proposed and utilised for setting up a 4 MTPA Pellet Plant at Konsari Maharashtra.  285.55 Cr was proposed for General Corporate Purposes and  16.32 Cr was proposed towards Issue Related Expenses. During the quarter ended 30 June 2026 utilisation was  916.13 Cr for the Pellet Plant  285.88 Cr for General Corporate Purposes and  15.99 Cr for Issue Related Expenses. Total utilisation was  1218 Cr with no unutilised amount. For the year ended 31 March 2026 total utilisation was  1217.67 Cr and  0.33 Cr remained unutilised. The unutilised amount was held in the ICICI Bank account and presented under Cash and Cash Equivalents as at 31 March 2026.16.Figures for the corresponding previous periods have been regrouped or reclassified wherever necessary to make them comparable.17. The Consolidated Financial Results for the quarter ended 30 June 2026 are available on the BSE India website at www bseindia com the NSE India website at www nseindia com and the Company website at www lloyds in.</in-capmkt:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock><in-capmkt:DescriptionOfOtherExpenses contextRef="OneExpenses1D">Mining, Royalty and Freight Expenses</in-capmkt:DescriptionOfOtherExpenses><in-capmkt:OtherExpenses contextRef="OneExpenses1D" decimals="-6" unitRef="INR">22673000000</in-capmkt:OtherExpenses><in-capmkt:DescriptionOfOtherExpenses contextRef="OneExpenses2D">Other Expenses</in-capmkt:DescriptionOfOtherExpenses><in-capmkt:OtherExpenses contextRef="OneExpenses2D" decimals="-5" unitRef="INR">6539800000</in-capmkt:OtherExpenses><in-capmkt: